{"t": 287.05, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FBR_Clamp", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails on S2 and S4 due to insufficient power and on S3 due to overvoltage and ripple. I am implementing a Parallel SSHI (Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor) circuit to invert the piezoelectric capacitance voltage at the peaks, significantly increasing the extracted power. To protect the load in S3, a Zener diode (DZ33) is added to clamp the output voltage at 3.3V. A large output capacitor is used to minimize ripple and stabilize the voltage for S5.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FBR_Clamp", "rationale": "The reference FBR fails on S2 and S4 due to insufficient power and on S3 due to overvoltage and ripple. I am implementing a Parallel SSHI (Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor) circuit to invert the piezoelectric capacitance voltage at the peaks, significantly increasing the extracted power. To protect the load in S3, a Zener diode (DZ33) is added to clamp the output voltage at 3.3V. A large output capacitor is used to minimize ripple and stabilize the voltage for S5.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.4e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}]}}
