{"t": 522.92, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FBR_LC_Filter", "rationale": "The previous SSHI-FBR design provided sufficient power (vavg) but suffered from high output ripple (vpp) and slow settling/startup (dv, tup) due to the trade-off in storage capacitor C1 size. By adding a filter inductor L2 between the rectifier bridge and the storage capacitor, we create an LC low-pass filter. This suppresses the high-current spikes inherent to the SSHI inversion process, allowing us to significantly reduce the value of C1. A smaller C1 will shorten the system time constant (tau = RL * C1), thereby improving startup time and settling behavior without sacrificing ripple performance.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FBR_LC_Filter", "rationale": "The previous SSHI-FBR design provided sufficient power (vavg) but suffered from high output ripple (vpp) and slow settling/startup (dv, tup) due to the trade-off in storage capacitor C1 size. By adding a filter inductor L2 between the rectifier bridge and the storage capacitor, we create an LC low-pass filter. This suppresses the high-current spikes inherent to the SSHI inversion process, allowing us to significantly reduce the value of C1. A smaller C1 will shorten the system time constant (tau = RL * C1), thereby improving startup time and settling behavior without sacrificing ripple performance.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n_filt"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "n_filt"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.4e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n_filt", "out"], "value